From: NTSD compatibility build
Subject: Windows: use instruction validation without page traps in full SMC mode

Full SMC mode validates each guest instruction in Core.cpp. Applying the
page-write traps as well changes guest-visible VirtualQuery/VirtualProtect
results, although the application has not changed its requested permissions.
Keep page trapping for mtrack; retain full instruction validation in full mode.

Also remove an interval from the writable/executable set when a caller changes
it to executable/read-only. Otherwise a later write fault can incorrectly be
treated as an internal SMC trap rather than a real guest protection violation.

This patch is maintained downstream for the NTSD runtime, not submitted to FEX.

diff --git a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
--- a/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/Common/InvalidationTracker.cpp
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
   : CTX {CTX}
   , Threads {Threads} {
   FEX_CONFIG_OPT(SMCChecks, SMCCHECKS);
-  SMCDetectionDisabled = (SMCChecks == FEXCore::Config::CONFIG_SMC_NONE);
+  SMCDetectionDisabled = (SMCChecks != FEXCore::Config::CONFIG_SMC_MTRACK);
 
   MEMORY_BASIC_INFORMATION Info;
   uint64_t Address = 0;
@@ -64,6 +64,8 @@
       if (EffectiveRWX) {
         LogMan::Msg::DFmt("Add SMC interval: {:X} - {:X}", AlignedBase, AlignedBase + AlignedSize);
         RWXIntervals.Insert(ProtInterval);
+      } else {
+        RWXIntervals.Remove(ProtInterval);
       }
       if (DEPDisabled && !HasExec) {
         DEPPromotedIntervals.Insert(ProtInterval);
